Here is the complete POST /api/owners create-owner chain, in execution order.

## 1. Controller method — POST /api/owners

The mapping is declared on the generated interface and implemented by the V1 controller.

- Route declaration: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java:52` (`PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"`) with `@RequestMapping(method = POST, value = "/owners", consumes/produces "application/json")` at lines 79-84. The parameter carries the request-body validation trigger (line 86):
  ```java
  default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
      @Parameter(...required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto)
  ```
  The interface is annotated `@Validated` (line 44), so `@Valid @RequestBody` drives Bean Validation on the DTO before the controller body runs.

- Class base path: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:54` — `@RequestMapping("/api")`, so effective path is `POST /api/owners`.

- Implementation, `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, lines 104-129:
  ```java
  @PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
  @Override
  public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
      HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
      Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
      Collection<Owner> owners = this.clinicService.findAllOwners();
      if (DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, java.time.LocalDate.now()) >= 100) {
          return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);
      }
      if (CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50) {
          return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
      }
      owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(owners,
          Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold()), owner));
      if (IdentityKeys.isDuplicate(owners, owner)) {
          return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
      }
      owner.setBulkSignupWarning(DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, java.time.LocalDate.now()) > 80);
      owner.setNamesakeCount(Namesakes.count(owners, owner));
      owner.assignCustomerCode(CityCodes.count(owners, owner) + 1);
      this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
      OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
      headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
          .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
      return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
  }
  ```
  Authorization: requires role `OWNER_ADMIN` (`@PreAuthorize`, line 104) before anything runs. Note: not `@Transactional` (unlike `deleteOwner`).

  Note there is also a V2 controller at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` but the endpoint you asked about (`POST /api/owners`) is the V1 one above.

## 2. Request DTO — `OwnerFieldsDto` with every validation annotation

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java` (generated from the OpenAPI spec).

Class-level custom constraint (line 28):
```java
@org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.validation.PostcodeValidation
public class OwnerFieldsDto {
```

Per-field constraints (annotations sit on the getters):
- `firstName` (line 74): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 95): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `address` (line 116): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*") @Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- `city` (line 137): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = ".*\\S.*") @Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- `telephone` (line 158): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^\\D*(\\d\\D*){10}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 20)` — i.e. exactly 10 digits after stripping non-digits
- `email` (line 179): `@Size(max = 255) @jakarta.validation.constraints.Email` (optional)
- `registrationDate` (line 200): `@Valid` (optional `LocalDate`, `@DateTimeFormat(iso = DATE)` on the field at line 43)
- `postcode` (line 221): `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$")` (optional)
- `sharesHousehold` (lines 233-247): `Boolean`, no validation annotations (controls the household-duplicate override; not persisted)

## 3. Custom class-level validator — `@PostcodeValidation`

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/PostcodeValidation.java`. The annotation (lines 27-34) is bound to `PostcodeRegionValidator` (same file, lines 37-57):
```java
public boolean isValid(OwnerFieldsDto owner, ConstraintValidatorContext context) {
    String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
    if (postcode == null || !postcode.matches("[0-9]{4}")) return true;
    int[] range = REGION_RANGE.get(Localities.regionOf(owner.getCity()));  // NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099
    if (range == null) return true;   // city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode
    int value = Integer.parseInt(postcode);
    return value >= range[0] && value <= range[1];
}
```
Region lookup here uses city only, via `Localities.regionOf(city)` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Localities.java:41`, table: Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD, else UNKNOWN).

If any Bean Validation constraint fails, the controller body is never entered; see the exception handler in section 7.

## 4. Mapping DTO → entity (transformations before business logic)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (lines 35-39) ignores `id` and `pets`, and applies two normalizers:
- `telephone` → `normalizeTelephone` → `E164.toE164(...)` (lines 42-45). `E164` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/E164.java:34`): strips non-digits; a leading `+` is kept as explicit country code, otherwise assumes AU `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; requires 8-15 national digits (AU must be 9), else throws `IllegalArgumentException`.
- `address` → `normalizeAddress` → `Addresses.normalize(...)` (lines 48-51). `Addresses` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Addresses.java:38`): trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE.

Also relevant: `Owner.setEmail` lower-cases the email (see entity, section 6). The mapper's `toOwnerDto` (lines 24-31) is called after save to build the response (computes displayName, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference, identityKey).

## 5. Controller business logic, side-effects, and thrown exceptions (exact order)

All helper classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/` (plus `IdentityKeys` in `util`). Order as executed in `addOwner`:

1. `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` — maps + normalizes telephone/address (may throw `IllegalArgumentException` from `E164`).
2. `clinicService.findAllOwners()` — loads all existing owners (used by every check below).
3. Daily limit — `DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, LocalDate.now()) >= 100` → returns **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**. `DailyRegistrations.countOn` (`DailyRegistrations.java:19`) rolls the day forward to a business day (`BusinessDays.rollForward`) and counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals it.
4. City cap — `CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50` → returns **409 CONFLICT**. `CityCodes.count` (`CityCodes.java:22`) counts existing owners with the same city (case-insensitive).
5. Set `householdId` — `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(owners, sharesHousehold, owner))`. `Households.householdId` (`Households.java:45`) returns `null` unless `sharesHousehold==true` AND an existing owner shares the normalized last name + address; otherwise a deterministic UUID derived from `lastName + "\n" + address`.
6. Duplicate identity — `IdentityKeys.isDuplicate(owners, owner)` → returns **409 CONFLICT**. `IdentityKeys` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/IdentityKeys.java`): the key is `telephone + "|" + email + "|" + householdId` (line 25); duplicate only when the whole key matches an existing owner. Because `householdId` was just set in step 5, joining a household changes the key.
7. Set `bulkSignupWarning` — `DailyRegistrations.countOn(...) > 80` (transient flag).
8. Set `namesakeCount` — `Namesakes.count(owners, owner)` (`Namesakes.java:22`), count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), transient.
9. Assign customer code — `owner.assignCustomerCode(CityCodes.count(owners, owner) + 1)`. `Owner.assignCustomerCode` (entity line 83) builds `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` from first 3 letters of city + first 3 of last name + zero-padded per-city sequence.
10. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — persist (section 6 lifecycle + section... below).
11. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` — build response body.
12. Set `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED**.

## 6. Entity, lifecycle callbacks, and audit listener

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`.
- `@Entity @Table(name="owners")` and `@EntityListeners(OwnerAuditListener.class)` (lines 37-39).
- Entity-level Bean Validation (checked at persist/flush time by Hibernate): `address` `@NotEmpty` (42), `city` `@NotEmpty` (46), `telephone` `@NotEmpty @Pattern("^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", "Telephone must be in E.164 format")` (50-51). Inherited from `Person` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`): `firstName` `@NotEmpty` (32-33), `lastName` `@NotEmpty` (36-37).
- `setEmail` (lines 128-131) stores email lower-cased.
- Transient fields (not persisted): `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning` (lines 88-119).
- `@PrePersist ensureRegistrationDate()` (lines 143-147): if `registrationDate` is null, default to `LocalDate.now()`, then roll forward to a business day via `BusinessDays.rollForward` (weekend → next Monday).
- `@PostPersist` audit hook: `OwnerAuditListener.onCreate` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/OwnerAuditListener.java:32-36`) logs to the `AUDIT` logger: `owner created id=… customerCode=… registrationDate=…`.

No application events are published anywhere in this chain (no `ApplicationEventPublisher` / `publishEvent` usage). The only "event"-like side effect is the `@PostPersist` audit log.

## Service and persistence layer

- Service: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java:234-237`:
  ```java
  public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
      ownerRepository.save(owner);
