## 4. Mapping DTO → entity (transformations before business logic)

File: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`. `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (lines 35-39) ignores `id` and `pets`, and applies two normalizers:
- `telephone` → `normalizeTelephone` → `E164.toE164(...)` (lines 42-45). `E164` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/E164.java:34`): strips non-digits; a leading `+` is kept as explicit country code, otherwise assumes AU `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; requires 8-15 national digits (AU must be 9), else throws `IllegalArgumentException`.
- `address` → `normalizeAddress` → `Addresses.normalize(...)` (lines 48-51). `Addresses` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Addresses.java:38`): trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE.

Also relevant: `Owner.setEmail` lower-cases the email (see entity, section 6). The mapper's `toOwnerDto` (lines 24-31) is called after save to build the response (computes displayName, membershipNumber, membershipLevel, locality, contactPreference, identityKey).

## 5. Controller business logic, side-effects, and thrown exceptions (exact order)

All helper classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/` (plus `IdentityKeys` in `util`). Order as executed in `addOwner`:

1. `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` — maps + normalizes telephone/address (may throw `IllegalArgumentException` from `E164`).
2. `clinicService.findAllOwners()` — loads all existing owners (used by every check below).
3. Daily limit — `DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, LocalDate.now()) >= 100` → returns **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**. `DailyRegistrations.countOn` (`DailyRegistrations.java:19`) rolls the day forward to a business day (`BusinessDays.rollForward`) and counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals it.
4. City cap — `CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50` → returns **409 CONFLICT**. `CityCodes.count` (`CityCodes.java:22`) counts existing owners with the same city (case-insensitive).
5. Set `householdId` — `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(owners, sharesHousehold, owner))`. `Households.householdId` (`Households.java:45`) returns `null` unless `sharesHousehold==true` AND an existing owner shares the normalized last name + address; otherwise a deterministic UUID derived from `lastName + "\n" + address`.
6. Duplicate identity — `IdentityKeys.isDuplicate(owners, owner)` → returns **409 CONFLICT**. `IdentityKeys` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/IdentityKeys.java`): the key is `telephone + "|" + email + "|" + householdId` (line 25); duplicate only when the whole key matches an existing owner. Because `householdId` was just set in step 5, joining a household changes the key.
7. Set `bulkSignupWarning` — `DailyRegistrations.countOn(...) > 80` (transient flag).
8. Set `namesakeCount` — `Namesakes.count(owners, owner)` (`Namesakes.java:22`), count of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive), transient.
9. Assign customer code — `owner.assignCustomerCode(CityCodes.count(owners, owner) + 1)`. `Owner.assignCustomerCode` (entity line 83) builds `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` from first 3 letters of city + first 3 of last name + zero-padded per-city sequence.
10. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` — persist (section 6 lifecycle + section... below).
11. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` — build response body.
12. Set `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 CREATED**.

